  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only multiprofile models are strong, especially scvi_n200, but image-only evidence is sparse and poor: resnet50 singleprofile has accuracy 0.208. It is unclear whether image features are uninformative or whether singleprofile/no aggregation is the bottleneck. config_011 tests the same resnet50 image encoder with multiprofile avgpool, the profile/aggregation setting that improved RNA-only PCA from 0.485 to 0.591, thereby isolating the effect of profile/aggregation for image. This is a simpler, high-information experiment than moving directly to multimodal fusion or changing the image encoder, and it clarifies whether resnet image profiles are worth including in later multimodal comparisons."
}

